{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":194147,"duration_api_ms":193149,"num_turns":32,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"605ab3a0-2df8-4d2d-afcb-5f824423ff0b","total_cost_usd":1.2943112499999998,"usage":{"input_tokens":1161,"cache_creation_input_tokens":81073,"cache_read_input_tokens":1169850,"output_tokens":7875,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":81073,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":1161,"outputTokens":7875,"cacheReadInputTokens":1169850,"cacheCreationInputTokens":81073,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.2943112499999998,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"amendments":[{"body":"In `legacy_process_param_normalization` (crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs:1192), the `_unit` parameter is accepted but completely ignored — normalization is purely name-based. This means if a developer attaches param_meta to `aob_k_tan_mg` with `unit = \"mg total\"` instead of `unit = \"mg N/L\"`, the system will still normalize the value to a concentration, creating a mismatch between the stated unit and the displayed value. Consider either (a) removing the unused `_unit` parameter to avoid implying it influences behavior, or (b) adding a debug assertion or warning when the attached unit doesn't match the expected normalization target (e.g., warn if a `_mg` legacy field has `unit` set to something other than a per-liter concentration).","rationale":"The normalization logic is correct today given the documented convention that `valid_range` should use normalized units. But the unused `_unit` parameter creates an implicit contract that unit-awareness exists when it doesn't, which could mislead a future contributor into thinking unit-conditional normalization is already handled. Since this is a scientific codebase where unit mismatches are high-severity, surfacing a diagnostic when the unit string and the name-based normalization disagree would be a low-cost safety net."}],"summary":"The provenance schema implementation is clean and correct. `ParamMeta` (crates/tank_core/src/types/provenance.rs) provides all required fields (unit, source, confidence, valid_range, notes) with proper serde attributes for optional loading. `ConfidenceLevel` is a validated enum that rejects unknown values at deserialization. Range checking produces warnings (not errors) as required. Legacy `_mg` fields are correctly normalized via `provenance_param_value` before range checks and display formatting (dividing by the 20L reference volume). Backward compatibility is ensured by `#[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = ...)]` on all `param_meta` maps. All 6 acceptance criteria tests pass, plus extensive additional coverage (unknown key rejection, non-finite values, invalid ranges, preset-level vs per-parameter confidence distinction, normalization display). The `deny_unknown_fields` on `ParamMeta` correctly prevents the `value` field from leaking into metadata sections. The `ParamMetaPreset` trait provides a clean abstraction for range checking and formatting across all preset types. Only one minor design concern identified (unused `_unit` parameter in normalization)."},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"294d2768-ef51-49c9-8017-4296814bab44"}
